# CVE-2025-71329 / CVE-2025-71330: image-size@1.2.1, a transitive dependency
# of metro@0.87.0 (the React Native/Expo bundler). Both are Denial-of-Service
# findings in image-size's dimension parser with no fixed version published
# upstream yet. This package only ever runs inside the developer/CI build
# pipeline (bundling this repository's own asset files); it never processes
# runtime, user-uploaded, or otherwise untrusted input -- production file
# uploads are a separate Go/R2 pipeline (M2 scope), not this Node bundler.
# Accepted residual risk, recorded in docs/security/threat-model.md; revisit
# when Renovate reports a fixed image-size release.
CVE-2025-71329
CVE-2025-71330

# CVE-2026-93687: braces@3.0.3, a stack-exhaustion denial of service in its
# recursive AST walkers. No fixed version is published upstream. It arrives
# only as app > @react-native/jest-preset > babel-jest > @jest/transform >
# micromatch > braces, a devDependency, expanding this repository's own Jest
# config globs rather than untrusted input; the worst outcome is a crashed
# test process, and the code never ships in a built artifact.
# Accepted residual risk, recorded as entry 4 in
# docs/security/threat-model.md; revisit when a fixed braces is published.
CVE-2026-93687

# CVE-2026-85393: node-forge@1.4.0, RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 signature verification
# accepting extra nested DigestAlgorithm elements, which allows forging
# signatures against low-exponent RSA keys. No fixed version is published
# upstream. This is a signature-verification bypass rather than a denial of
# service, and it arrives through expo, a production dependency, so the
# acceptance rests on reachability and was verified rather than assumed: no
# first-party source imports node-forge, and @expo/cli only references it
# from two code-signing utilities that run on a developer machine or in CI.
# The Expo Updates manifest-signing path, the one that would perform the
# vulnerable verification, is not configured here (no expo-updates or EAS
# package, no eas.json, no updates/codeSigning/runtimeVersion key in
# app/app.json). Accepted residual risk, recorded as entry 5 in
# docs/security/threat-model.md, WITH A MANDATORY RE-EVALUATION TRIGGER:
# adopting expo-updates code signing or an EAS Update pipeline puts this
# code path into use and invalidates the acceptance.
CVE-2026-85393
